# The root set den's TLS (wolf-std's public-PKI client) trusts on PAX
# (px104, R-px104-2): /etc/ssl/certs/ca-roots.der, the concatenated DER
# certificates den reads through DEN_TLS_ROOTS (/etc/shrc exports it) or
# --tls-roots. den reads no system store of its own.
#
# The source: Mozilla's root store (NSS's certdata.txt, the CA certificates
# Mozilla trusts for TLS servers), as curl extracts it to PEM, dated
# 2026-10-20 ("Certificate data from Mozilla as of: Tue Oct 20 13:32:40 2026
# GMT", mk-ca-bundle.pl 1.35), 118 certificates; ROOTS_REV names it in
# /etc/pax-release. Licence: the Mozilla
# Public License 2.0, as Mozilla publishes certdata.txt (curl's page,
# https://curl.se/docs/caextract.html, says so). tools/mkroots fetches the
# PEM by this name, refuses it unless both reads of its sha256 are
# ROOTS_PEM_SHA256 (curl's own published .sha256 says the same), converts
# it with an RFC 7468 decoder of PAX's own, and refuses the result unless
# it is ROOTS_COUNT certificates whose bytes have ROOTS_DER_SHA256 (and,
# where openssl is on PATH, the same bytes as `openssl x509 -outform DER`
# of each certificate, concatenated). A new set is a new date here.
ROOTS_REV=cacert-2026-10-20
ROOTS_URL=https://curl.se/ca/cacert-2026-10-20.pem
ROOTS_PEM_SHA256=796f1389bfea13c0ed78f663b765baaff54a508e5483786bd6ece73c5e3e3cbe
ROOTS_COUNT=118
ROOTS_DER_SHA256=7a713f238d42397d0360c7f8523d45bedee6824f583372d6afd96a129ea5c1f1
